An application programming interface (API) is a set of commands, functions, protocols, and objects that programmers can use to create software or interact with an external system
The website is like a restaurant, where the data that powers these websites are the kitchen. Apis are like the menu.
API endpoint is the location of where the data is stored. Usually just a URL.
